# Copy to .env only to override a default — unlike apps/api/.env, nothing here is required and the
# app runs from a clean clone without this file.
#
# Both variables are read at *build* time, not at boot: Vite substitutes them into the bundle, so a
# changed value needs a rebuild rather than a restart. That is the opposite of the API's contract,
# where every variable is read per process start.

# --- Dev server -------------------------------------------------------------
# Where `vite dev` proxies /api. Keeping the browser on one origin in development means no CORS
# round-trip, so the dev setup cannot pass while a deployed one fails on a preflight.
# Only the dev server reads it: `vite build` never evaluates the `server` block.
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:3000

# --- Production build -------------------------------------------------------
# Origin of the API, *without* the /api prefix — src/api/client.ts appends API_PREFIX itself.
#
# Left unset on purpose when the API answers on the same origin as this app: the empty default
# makes every request a relative /api path, which is the only form that survives a host handing out
# a new hostname per build (BR-100). A baked-in absolute URL would point every preview build at
# whichever environment was named here.
#
# Set it only when the API is a separate origin.
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com
